<title>GERMANY: HOCKEY-WOMEN'S CHAMPIONS' TROPHY RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HOCKEY-WOMEN'S CHAMPIONS' TROPHY RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the women's</p>
<p>Champions' Trophy hockey tournament on Wednesday:</p>
<p>Netherlands 3 United States 0 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Fleur van de Kieft 5, 13, Suzan van der Wielen 53</p>
<p>Germany 3 South Korea 2 (halftime 2-2).</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Germany - Nadine Ernsting-Krienke 4, Denise Klecker 16, Heike</p>
<p>Latzsch 54.</p>
<p>South Korea - Choi Mi-soon 11, Park Eun-kyung 32.</p>
<p>Australia 3 Britain 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Karen Smith 20, Jennifer Morris 28, Michelle</p>
<p>Andrews 50</p>
<p>    Standings	P  W  D  L  F  A Pts</p>
<p> 1. Australia	3  2  1  0  6  1  7</p>
<p> 2. Netherlands    3  2  0  1  4  2  6</p>
<p> 3. Germany	  3  1  2  0  6  5  5</p>
<p>4. United States  3  1  1  1  3  5  4</p>
<p> 5. South Korea    3  1  0  2  4  4  3</p>
<p> 6. Britain	  3  0  0  3  0  6  0</p>
